Package: picache
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: systemd (>= 247), init-system-helpers, passwd, ca-certificates
Suggests: cifs-utils, nfs-common
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Hustenreizjuengling/PiCache
Description: filtering DNS server and download cache for the home network
 PiCache filters DNS for every device of the network with blocklists and
 rules, adds parental controls, local DNS records, encrypted DNS and an
 optional DHCP server, and caches game and operating system downloads for
 the whole network. One static program with an embedded web UI; it runs
 unprivileged as the system user picache in a hardened systemd unit.
 .
 The web UI listens on port 8080 (HTTPS: 8443). The one-time setup token of
 the first start: sudo picache setup-token
